  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Suppose we have events $A,B\\subset\\Omega$ with $\\Pr(B)\\ne0$. Prove that\n$$\\Pr(A'\\mid B)=1-\\Pr(A\\mid B).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\Pr(A'\\mid B)=\\dfrac{\\Pr(B)-\\Pr(A\\cap B)}{\\Pr(B)}=1-\\Pr(A\\mid B)$.\n\nThe disjoint events $A\\cap B$ and $A'\\cap B$ partition $B$.",
      "worked": "The events $A\\cap B$ and $A'\\cap B$ are disjoint and their union is $B$, so $\\Pr(A'\\cap B)=\\Pr(B)-\\Pr(A\\cap B)$. Since $\\Pr(B)\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\Pr(A'\\mid B)&=\\frac{\\Pr(A'\\cap B)}{\\Pr(B)}\\\\\n\\Pr(A'\\mid B)&=\\frac{\\Pr(B)-\\Pr(A\\cap B)}{\\Pr(B)}\\\\\n\\Pr(A'\\mid B)&=1-\\frac{\\Pr(A\\cap B)}{\\Pr(B)}\\\\\n\\Pr(A'\\mid B)&=1-\\Pr(A\\mid B).\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
